  "scorer_rule_differences": {
    "default_argument_credit": "v2 rule V2b drops a predicted argument key absent from every same-tool gold call when its value equals that tool's registry default; the official scorer counts every extra key as a parameter error and therefore as an exact-match failure",
    "first_call_only_vs_ordered_sequence": "the official HF path never populates all_tool_calls, so the official scorer reads only the FIRST parsed call against the PRIMARY gold tool, while a2t-toolcall-v2 compares the whole ordered predicted sequence with the whole expected sequence",
    "numeric_and_boolean_coercion": "v2 rule V2d compares a numeric-looking string to its numeric value and 'true'/'false' to the matching boolean; the official normalize_parameters reaches a similar place by a different route, so this rule rarely separates the two alone",
    "parameter_f1_definition": "the official parameter F1 is a macro average of per-sample key P/R/F1 while v2's slot F1 is micro over (tool, key, value) triples, so the two answer different questions and are reported side by side rather than differenced",
    "primary_gold_tool_vs_full_expected_sequence": "official gold is the release's QuerySample (primary tool_name + verbatim extracted_params); v2 gold is a2t-gold-v1, which builds the full expected call sequence and may take primary arguments from the expected_tool_call call string"
  },
